ish from Cinema 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" aria-current=\"page\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"verse-viewer-one-tag-any-page\"><code>&lt;verse-viewer&gt;</code>: one tag, any page<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#verse-viewer-one-tag-any-page\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Put a Verse scene on any page that renders HTML with one tag. The poster paints at once; the 3D engine loads when the card scrolls into view, on tap, or straight away. No headers to set on your site: the engine runs on the Verse origin, inside the card.</p>\n<p><strong>Status:</strong> tested. The element is proven in a real browser on a third-party origin (<code>web/test/fix-verify-integrations.mjs</code>: self-registration, lazy / eager loading, live attributes, the <code>viewer()</code> upgrade to the embed SDK) and by its unit tests (<code>sdk/viewer</code>, <code>npm test</code>). The npm package <code>@ctruhtech/verse-viewer</code> is built but <strong>not yet published</strong>; until it is, load it from the Verse server as below.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-the-tag\">1. The tag<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#1-the-tag\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"html\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-html\">&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot; src=&quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/sdk/verse-viewer.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n\n&lt;verse-viewer src=&quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/?vpk=ingest/palm-villa-0a1b2c3d4e5f.vpk&quot;&gt;&lt;/verse-viewer&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<p>That is all. <code>src</code> is the share link from Studio (Studio → Share, or Studio → Embed for a private scene: the link then carries its share token). Any knob on the share link — <code>look</code>, <code>bg</code>, <code>view</code>, <code>variant</code>, <code>cfg</code>, <code>share</code> — carries over.</p>\n<p>The element is <code>display: block; width: 100%</code>. Size it like an image: give it a width, or let it fill its column, and the box follows the aspect ratio.</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-from-npm-bundlers-frameworks\">2. From npm (bundlers, frameworks)<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#2-from-npm-bundlers-frameworks\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-2\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">npm install @ctruhtech/verse-viewer</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-3\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">import &quot;@ctruhtech/verse-viewer/register&quot;;          // defines &lt;verse-viewer&gt;; a no-op on a server</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or without the side effect:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-4\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">import { defineVerseViewer } from &quot;@ctruhtech/verse-viewer&quot;;\ndefineVerseViewer();</code></pre></div>\n<p>Svelte, Angular, Lit, Astro, Qwik: use the tag directly (Angular: add <code>CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA</code>). React and Vue have typed wrappers: <a href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue\">React and Vue</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-attributes\">3. Attributes<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#3-attributes\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Values</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>src</code></td><td>share link · embed URL · <code>https://HOST/ingest/&lt;id&gt;.vpk</code> · <code>ingest/&lt;id&gt;.vpk</code> · a scene id</td><td>What to show.</td></tr><tr><td><code>scene</code></td><td>scene id</td><td>The same as <code>src</code> with a bare id.</td></tr><tr><td><code>server</code></td><td>origin</td><td>The Verse origin. Default: the origin of an absolute <code>src</code>, else <code>https://verse.ctruh.com</code>. Set it for a self-hosted server.</td></tr><tr><td><code>poster</code></td><td>image URL</td><td>Shown before the engine arrives. Default: the scene&#39;s own poster.</td></tr><tr><td><code>loading</code></td><td><code>lazy</code> (default) · <code>eager</code> · <code>tap</code></td><td>When the 3D loads: when the card is in view · at once · when tapped. Use <code>tap</code> on a page with several scenes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>aspect</code></td><td><code>16:9</code> (default) · <code>4:3</code> · <code>1:1</code> · <code>3:4</code> · <code>9:16</code> · <code>21:9</code></td><td>The box&#39;s shape. Fidelity products default to <code>1:1</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>background</code></td><td><code>rrggbb</code> · <code>transparent</code> · <code>grad:a,b</code> · <code>studio:warm</code> …</td><td>The backdrop (the share link&#39;s <code>bg</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>camera</code></td><td>a saved view name · <code>overview</code></td><td>The starting camera (the share link&#39;s <code>view</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>look</code> / <code>variant</code> / <code>cfg</code> / <code>share</code></td><td></td><td>Look preset · material variant · configurator selection · a private scene&#39;s share token.</td></tr><tr><td><code>analytics</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Count nothing from this embed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ar</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Hide the View in AR control (shown by default where the phone can place the scene).</td></tr><tr><td><code>guard</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>The scene takes every gesture at once. Default: a vertical swipe and the mouse wheel scroll your page until the visitor taps or clicks into the scene.</td></tr><tr><td><code>fullscreen</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Hide the fullscreen button.</td></tr><tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>text</td><td>The frame&#39;s accessible name. Default: &quot;&lt;Scene name&gt; — 3D view&quot;.</td></tr><tr><td><code>api</code></td><td>present</td><td>Upgrade to the embed SDK as soon as the element connects (section 5).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Every attribute is live: change it and the card re-renders with the new URL.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"html\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-5\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-html\">&lt;verse-viewer src=&quot;…&quot; loading=&quot;tap&quot; aspect=&quot;4:3&quot; look=&quot;studio:warm&quot; analytics=&quot;false&quot; title=&quot;Villa, living room&quot;&gt;&lt;/verse-viewer&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"4-styling\">4. Styling<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#4-styling\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"css\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-6\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-css\">verse-viewer { max-width: 960px; --verse-viewer-radius: 12px; --verse-viewer-background: #0b0d12; }\nverse-viewer::part(box) { box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, .3); }</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>--verse-viewer-radius</code> rounds the card; <code>--verse-viewer-background</code> is the colour behind the poster while it loads; <code>::part(box)</code> is the sized box around the frame.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-the-programmatic-api\">5. The programmatic API<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#5-the-programmatic-api\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<p><code>element.viewer()</code> loads <code>&lt;server&gt;/embed.js</code> once and replaces the card with the embed SDK&#39;s own mount: the full <a href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk\">embed SDK</a> (<code>pick</code>, <code>setVariant</code>, <code>setConfiguration</code>, <code>enterAR</code>, <code>exportVideo</code>, every event). SDK events are also re-dispatched on the element as <code>verse-&lt;name&gt;</code> CustomEvents, so a framework can listen without touching the API.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-7\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const el = document.querySelector(&quot;verse-viewer&quot;);\nel.addEventListener(&quot;verse-load&quot;, (e) =&gt; console.log(&quot;card loaded&quot;, e.detail.id));\nconst viewer = await el.viewer();\nviewer.on(&quot;loaded&quot;, (d) =&gt; console.log(d.clusters, &quot;clusters&quot;));\nawait viewer.setVariant(&quot;Oak&quot;);</code></pre></div>\n<p>Properties: <code>element.embedUrl</code> (the URL the card shows), <code>element.sceneId</code>, <code>element.src</code>, <code>element.loading</code>.</p>\n<p>Add the <code>api</code> attribute to upgrade on connect instead of on the first <code>viewer()</code> call; the card&#39;s laziness is lost, so use it only where the page exists for the scene.</p>\n<h2 id=\"6-server-side-rendering\">6. Server-side rendering<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#6-server-side-rendering\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-7\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Importing <code>@ctruhtech/verse-viewer</code> or <code>@ctruhtech/verse-viewer/register</code> on a server does nothing (there is no <code>window</code>). Render the tag with its attributes as HTML and the browser upgrades it when the module runs.</p>\n<p>Two helpers for places that cannot run JavaScript (emails, AMP, RSS, a no-JS fallback):</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-8\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">import { renderStaticHtml, buildEmbedUrl } from &quot;@ctruhtech/verse-viewer&quot;;\nrenderStaticHtml({ src, aspect: &quot;16:9&quot; });   // the documented responsive &lt;iframe&gt;\nbuildEmbedUrl({ src, loading: &quot;tap&quot; });      // the embed URL alone</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"7-self-hosted-servers\">7. Self-hosted servers<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#7-self-hosted-servers\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-8\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Point <code>server</code> at your origin, or use an absolute <code>src</code> from it (<code>src=&quot;https://verse.example.com/?vpk=ingest/&lt;id&gt;.vpk&quot;</code>): the module itself can be loaded from any Verse server (<code>&lt;your origin&gt;/sdk/verse-viewer.js</code>) or from npm. The embed card, the poster, the engine and <code>embed.js</code> all come from the server named in <code>src</code> / <code>server</code>, never from <code>verse.ctruh.com</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"questions\">Questions<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#questions\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-9\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Does the element need any header on my site?</strong> No. The engine runs inside the Verse frame. A site that is itself cross-origin isolated (COOP / COEP) works too.</li><li><strong>Does it count views?</strong> Yes, as <em>Arrived via: embed</em> in Analytics, unless <code>analytics=&quot;false&quot;</code>.</li><li><strong>Can I use the plain iframe instead?</strong> Yes: Studio → Embed copies it, and <code>renderStaticHtml()</code> returns the same markup. The element adds live attributes, the SDK upgrade and the framework wrappers.</li><li><strong>Which browsers?</strong> Every browser that runs the viewer (<a href=\"/docs/browser-support\" id=\"lnk-browser-support-3\">Browser support</a>); the element itself needs custom elements and shadow DOM, which all current browsers have.</li></ul>\n<p>See also: <a href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere\">Embed anywhere</a> (WordPress, Shopify, Webflow), <a href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-embed-the-viewer\">Embed the viewer</a> (the iframe and the SDK), <a href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations\">Integrations</a> (the full matrix).</p></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#1-the-tag\" id=\"lnk-1-the-tag\">1. The tag</a><a href=\"#2-from-npm-bundlers-frameworks\" id=\"lnk-2-from-npm-bundlers-frameworks\">2. From npm (bundlers, frameworks)</a><a href=\"#3-attributes\" id=\"lnk-3-attributes\">3. Attributes</a><a href=\"#4-styling\" id=\"lnk-4-styling\">4. Styling</a><a href=\"#5-the-programmatic-api\" id=\"lnk-5-the-programmatic-api\">5. The programmatic API</a><a href=\"#6-server-side-rendering\" id=\"lnk-6-server-side-rendering\">6. Server-side rendering</a><a href=\"#7-self-hosted-servers\" id=\"lnk-7-self-hosted-servers\">7. Self-hosted servers</a><a href=\"#questions\" id=\"lnk-questions\">Questions</a></aside></section>"}